---

## Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · .NET 10.0  
**Catalog:** testsmells.org 19-smell taxonomy (Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020)  
**Integration calibration applied:** Class is marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### ❶ Conditional Test Logic — **High**

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 96)  
**Not downgraded:** Integration calibration only applies to Mystery Guest, Eager Test, and Sleepy Test.

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);   // path A
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);       // path B
}
```

**Problem:** Only one branch ever executes per run. If the type hierarchy changes, one assertion silently disappears. This is a hidden testing gap.

**Fix:** Split into two tests with deterministic setup:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<PremiumUser>(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(((PremiumUser)loaded).DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — you can't tell which branch runs in CI.

---

#### ❷ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — **High**

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion
}
```

**Problem:** This test passes even if `Insert` silently drops every record. MSTest reports it green as long as no exception is thrown.

**Fix:** Assert on the observable outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False pass — 100 % coverage with 0 % verification.

---

#### ❸ Sleepy Test — **Medium** *(downgraded from High; integration context)*

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);   // blocks for 3 seconds

Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Problem:** Adds 3 s of wall-clock time per run, and the delay is a guess — too short on slow CI, wastefully long on fast machines. Even for integration tests this is a reliability hazard.

**Fix:** Poll with a timeout instead:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within the timeout.");
}

private static async Task<bool> WaitUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI; slow feedback loop (Camara et al., SAST 2021 links Sleepy Test to flakiness).

---

#### ❹ Assertion Roulette — **Medium**

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);           // which failed?
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);       // 4 assertions, 0 messages
```

**Problem:** 4 assertions with no message parameters. When one fails, the MSTest output says _"Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<(null)>."_ — you must read the source to know it was the `Name` check.

**Fix:** Add message parameters:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned on insert.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slow diagnosis — developers must open the source file on every CI failure.

