### Smells Scanned & Not Found (15 / 19 clean ✔)

| Smell | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Mystery Guest | ✔ Clean | In-memory SQLite — no external files/services |
| Eager Test | ✔ Clean | No test calls 4+ distinct production methods |
| Magic Number Test | ✔ Clean | All numeric literals are contextually obvious (e.g., `3` after inserting 3 items) |
| Sensitive Equality | ✔ Clean | No `ToString()`-based comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✔ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks |
| General Fixture | ✔ Clean | Both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✔ Clean | No `[Ignore]` attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✔ Clean | No identical assertion pairs |
| Lazy Test | ✔ Clean | Each test targets a distinct behavior |
| Constructor Initialization | ✔ Clean | Uses `[TestInitialize]` properly |
| Default Test | ✔ Clean | Meaningful class name |
| Redundant Print | ✔ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` |
| Redundant Assertion | ✔ Clean | No tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✔ Clean | In-memory DB created per-test |
| Empty Test | ✔ Clean | All methods have executable code |

### Smell-Free Highlights

`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`, and `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` are well-structured: clear arrange/act/assert, meaningful names, proper assertions, and no smells.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** (`BulkInsert`) | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` | ~1 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** (`GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`) | Split into 2 deterministic tests | ~10 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** (`NotifyOnInsert`) | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-with-timeout | ~15 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** (`InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`) | Add message strings to 4 assertions | ~2 min |

Priorities 1–2 eliminate **false-pass risk** (tests that look green but verify nothing or only half the behavior). Priority 3 reduces **flakiness**. Priority 4 is a **quality-of-life** improvement for CI failure diagnosis.
